= Technology Option - Consent-gated matching (selected) [TECH-05] =

**Report Format:** §1.3 Technology

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|TECH-05
|Name|Consent-gated matching (selected)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Group reasoning; HFC-15.
|Category|AI/ICT
|Capabilities|(((
Finds pairs of residents who share released items: a place, a trade, an interest, a past tie. A pair is suggested only if:

1. each item used was released by its owner, privately
1. the relationship map allows the pair: no known conflict, no off-limits topic
1. the coordinator approves the suggestion

Health, losses and family conflicts are never matching items. Unknown pair, or a map change awaiting review: no suggestion. Audit: item IDs only.

Relationship map, per resident: sensitive topics, each with trusted persons and the agreed approach. Per pair: date introduced; off-limits topics; "again" or "not again" after each meeting. Kept by ST-05 with ST-04 and family; reviewed after any death, diagnosis, conflict or move.
)))
|Limitations|The map is only as current as staff keep it. Matching on listed facts misses friendships that no profile predicts.
|Maturity and feasibility|Medium; simple rules, careful upkeep.
|Failure and fallback behaviour|Matching fails: staff introduce residents as today, without suggestions.
|Benefits|HV-06: introductions on common ground. HV-03: nothing used without consent.
|Drawbacks|Strains VT-01. Upkeep for ST-05.
|Selected or rejected|Selected.

== Graph edges ==

enables → F1, F2, F3; addresses → HV-03, HV-06; strains → VT-01.

= Technology Option - Resident profile for matching (selected) [TECH-06] =

**Report Format:** §1.3 Technology

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|TECH-06
|Name|Resident profile for matching (selected)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Group reasoning; HFC-04, HFC-15. Life-story work is common practice in dementia care.
|Category|AI/ICT
|Capabilities|(((
Per resident:

* Life story: places lived, work, church or clubs, family as the resident tells it, important events
* Preferences: activities, time of day, one person or a group, indoors or out
* Past ties: people in the home known from before
* For each item: shareable or private; source (resident, relative, staff); date last checked

Entered with the resident and family at the life-story interview (SA-01); the resident and representative can see and change it. Pepper speaks only prepared, checked lines ("Elena, this is Jan. You both worked at the post office in [town]."); no text is generated.
)))
|Limitations|Relatives' memories can be wrong or out of date. Items in a resident's own words are hard to match automatically; the coordinator matches those by hand.
|Maturity and feasibility|Medium; a form and a database.
|Failure and fallback behaviour|No profile: no suggestions for that resident; staff introduce them as today.
|Benefits|HV-07: introductions built on the resident's own life. HV-06: common ground.
|Drawbacks|Strains VT-05: a rich profile is a privacy risk.
|Selected or rejected|Selected.

== Graph edges ==

enables → F2, F3; addresses → HV-06, HV-07; strains → VT-01, VT-05.

= Technology Option - Cloud speech and language services (rejected) [TECH-07] =

**Report Format:** §1.3 Technology

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|TECH-07
|Name|Cloud speech and language services (rejected)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Group reasoning.
|Category|AI/ICT
|Capabilities|Better speech recognition; generated introductions; matching by a language model.
|Limitations|Needs an internet connection.
|Maturity and feasibility|High.
|Failure and fallback behaviour|Not applicable - rejected.
|Benefits|HV-06: understands more, says more and finds less obvious matches.
|Drawbacks|Profiles and answers leave the home (HV-03). A generated sentence can be untrue about a resident's life, and cannot be checked before it is said (HV-08).
|Selected or rejected|Rejected.

