= Technology Option - Location and body sensing (rejected) [TECH-09] =

**Report Format:** §1.3 Technology

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|TECH-09
|Name|Location and body sensing: GPS, cameras, wristbands (rejected)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Commercially common. Concerns reviewed in Niemeijer et al. (2010).
|Category|Sensing / Wearable
|Capabilities|Position anywhere in the home; faces and distress; heart rate and activity.
|Limitations|Continuous monitoring.
|Maturity and feasibility|High.
|Failure and fallback behaviour|Not applicable - rejected.
|Benefits|HV-04: finds a resident anywhere. HV-05: sees distress that staff miss.
|Drawbacks|Felt as surveillance; violates HV-03. The one remaining need, noticing withdrawal, is met by opt-in presence counts (TECH-03); distress is left to people.
|Selected or rejected|Rejected.

